# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
#
# style.css is served with a long browser-cache TTL by default (max-age=14400,
# i.e. 4 hours). On a site that gets edited frequently that means a visitor can
# keep rendering a stale stylesheet for hours after a deploy — new HTML arrives
# but the old CSS is still applied, so layout changes appear not to have shipped.
#
# Force revalidation on every load instead. The browser still sends
# If-None-Match and gets a cheap 304 when the file is unchanged, so this costs
# almost nothing on a static site while guaranteeing edits are picked up
# immediately.
#
# Keep this file in the repo root (Cloudflare Pages reads it at deploy time).
# If a future stylesheet or script is added and should never be stale, add its
# path here the same way.

/style.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
